<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fluvià</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fluvia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fluvià is a river in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a> in Catalonia, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, about 97 kilometres long. It rises in the volcanic district of La Garrotxa, flows past the medieval town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a> and reaches the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-roses">Gulf of Roses</a>, near the ancient Greek trading town of Emporion, now Empúries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fluvia.jpg" alt="Fluvià" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_del_riu_Fluvi%C3%A0_a_Sant_Pere_Pescador.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
